[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624916357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2624916357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2624916357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cdQuF","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T16:06:03Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T16:06:03Z","body":"> Wanted to take a quick look through this. Looks cool and makes sense to me! Would be curious to try this out with a relevant API sometime but in the spec it looks like it's only used by Magic Leap currently?\r\n\r\nIt's used by a number of APIs still in development, but it will be some time before those are public.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624916357/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688441647","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2688441647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2688441647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gPl0v","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T16:13:59Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T16:22:57Z","body":"As part of the change to have `OpenXRExtensionWrapper` be an `Object`, there's a couple other changes that I personally think we should make:\r\n\r\n1. **Merge the methods from `OpenXRCompositionLayerProvider` up into `OpenXRExtensionWrapper`.** While using `OpenXRCompositionLayerProvider` like a C#/Java/PHP/etc `interface` makes sense, multiple inheritance in C++ can cause weird issues especially in conjunction with Godot's `Object` and `ClassDB` system. I forget the issue and PR numbers, but in the past we had a really hard to debug crash that was the result of this, and I personally think it would be better to avoid the problem entirely by just not using multiple inheritance. (Also, we had some later work that attempted to follow the example of `OpenXRCompositionLayerProvider` and my review was \"let's not do that anymore\" because of these issues, but I worry that future contributors may still see `OpenXRCompositionLayerProvider` and again try to follow its example, so let's just get it out of there)\r\n2. **Deprecated `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension` in favor of just using the now-exposed `OpenXRExtensionWrapper`.** We can do this without breaking compatibility by just making the default implementations of the virtual methods on `OpenXRExtensionWrapper` use the GDExtension implementations from `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension`, and emptying out `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension` but not removing it. Old GDExtensions would still extend `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension` and continue working fine, but newer GDExtensions could directly extend `OpenXRExtensionWrapper`. This will eliminate the annoying extension-extension we have in `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension` :-)\r\n\r\nMaybe it makes sense to spin the \"`OpenXRExtensionWrapper` becomes an `Object`\" part of this into its own PR to focus on that? Or, if we think this one is ready to merge when the Godot 4.5 dev cycle opens up, I could do the other changes I describe above as a follow-up PR?\r\n\r\n**UPDATE:** The crash related to multiple inheritance that I was referring to in point nr 1 was issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/88613 fixed by PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/88689","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688441647/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692665423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2692665423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2692665423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gftBP","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T10:31:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T10:31:13Z","body":"@dsnopek the crash issues were caused by a moving pointer between the different classes because of late introduction of a v-table.\r\nThis is fixed by making sure the primary base class has a virtual destructor. We dealt with that.\r\n\r\nMy main worry with point 1 is that we'll end up looping through all wrappers just to find out only one or two actually have compositor logic.\r\n\r\nFor point 2, it's definitely worth doing a follow up to clean up `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension` however it has become the norm to always implement a `*Extension` class for exposure to GDExtension and keep the base class abstract.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692665423/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692721782","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2692721782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2692721782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gf6x2","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T13:03:49Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T13:03:49Z","body":"> My main worry with point 1 is that we'll end up looping through all wrappers just to find out only one or two actually have compositor logic.\r\n\r\nI'm not saying to get rid of the registration for the extensions that affect compositor layers. Just that it would take `OpenXRExtensionWrapper *` rather than `OpenXRCompositionLayerProvider *`. Take a look at `register_projection_views_extension()` - for that one we're also doing a registration, but we didn't make a new  base class for it.\r\n\r\n> however it has become the norm to always implement a `*Extension` class for exposure to GDExtension and keep the base class abstract.\r\n\r\nWe do it both ways for different things in Godot.\r\n\r\nThe only advantage of keeping it abstract (as opposed to virtual) is that users could try to extend `OpenXRExtensionWrapper` in GDScript, which won't work because of all the pointer arguments. But we already have the risk, because they could try to do the same with `OpenXRExtensionWrapperExtension`, and I've never heard of anyone trying to do that. It's really only changing which class name carries the risk.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692721782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720155738","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2720155738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2720155738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iIkha","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T06:52:04Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T06:52:04Z","body":"Ok, I've made this ready for proper review. Been testing this for the past few weeks and it is working fine. Sadly can't share the project I'm working on just yet.\r\n\r\nI did change things so it properly uses `XrFutureEXT` internally and the class methods used by extension in the core can use this type, but the functions exposed to GDExtension and GDScript use `uint64_t`. Much clearer implementation.\r\n\r\n@dsnopek I've left the classes as they are for now, I do think we need to look into this further but changing those would be serious breaking changes, especially the *extension change. I do hear what you're saying here though so far in all my discussions with the core team I get two answers, some always wanting the specific extension classes and others saying its find to just make the base class virtual. I'm not bothered one way or the other.\r\n\r\nBut changing it now will break our existing vendor extension and I think that's not worth it. Also it will require a bunch of other cleanup that I'd rather do in a separate PR if we decide to go down this route.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720155738/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721526737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2721526737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2721526737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iNzPR","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T14:46:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T14:46:56Z","body":"@BastiaanOlij:\r\n\r\n> I do think we need to look into this further but changing those would be serious breaking changes, especially the *extension change.\r\n[...]\r\n> But changing it now will break our existing vendor extension and I think that's not worth it.\r\n\r\nI'm happy to make a follow-up PR! However, the changes I described above would not be breaking changes - they should be fully backwards compatible. The vendor extension should be able to keep working without any changes\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721526737/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2723831071","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101951#issuecomment-2723831071","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101951","id":2723831071,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iWl0f","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/user